<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">ArcelorMittal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2006</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">ArcelorMittal is a multinational <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> and mining company formed in 2006 when Mittal Steel took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcelor">Arcelor</a>. Headquartered in Luxembourg, it is one of the largest steel producers in the world, with plants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. It continues the industrial tradition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arbed">ARBED</a>, long the dominant firm in the Luxembourg economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arcelormittal.jpg" alt="ArcelorMittal" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meffo · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ArcelorMittalLuxemburg.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
